== CASE ==
AWPTCM-T44276  (208) Authentication&Security_WebAuthentication - DHCP Server for Web Authentication
ck.db (read at triage, queue lines 112-129): Status Draft; objective, precondition and steps NOT authored
(one empty step). Run from its title, per the triage plan: `auth-web-server dhcp ipaddress <net>` + `lease`;
an unauthenticated client (dhcp4.py client, crafted at L2, no host IP change) must be OFFERed/ACKed an address
with the configured lease (opt 51) by the DUT; then login from eth6's own MAC; a second client MAC for
multi-supplicant DHCP. The second-MAC *browse* leg needs D2 (root on tb5): out of scope, not measured.
References: AW+ Command Reference 5.5.6-1 "auth-web-server dhcp ipaddress" (enables the DHCP service of the
Web-Authentication server; "You cannot use the IPv4 address assigned to the device's interface as the
Web-Authentication server address"; example 10.0.0.1/8); AAA and Port Authentication Feature Overview and
Configuration Guide C613-22088-00 rev P p.42-43 ("There is a DHCP server built in to web authentication ...
dedicated to serving IP addresses to be used by web authentication clients"; default lease 30 s, range 20-60;
the dhcp address must equal an already-configured auth-web-server ipaddress).
